  "official_explanations": {
    "general_header_html": "<p class=\"alert info\">This event occurred about three hours after the \n\n<a href=\"https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/eventpage/us7000tbwb/executive\">\n  landslide that triggered catastrophic flooding in Nepal and China\n</a>\n\n. It was identified during post-processing of low-frequency seismic records and shows characteristics consistent with a landslide. Due to the lack of high-frequency energy, the location of this event was estimated from satellite images.\n\nFor more information see the\n<a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/landslide-hazards/science/2026-nepal-debris-avalanche-and-flash-flood\">\nUSGS landslides special event page. \n</a>\n\n</p>",
    "impact_text": "A second landslide event following M 5.2 at 02:52 UTC. This event created a temporary dam and lake on the Trishuli River. The landslide location was obtained from satellite imagery.\n"
  },
  "mechanism_evidence": "USGS post-processing of low-frequency records found characteristics consistent with landslide; no high-frequency energy; later event described as forming a temporary Trishuli River dam/lake",
